          "text": "My mother, Katsuye Furuyama, arrived from Fukushima Japan, in 1932 as a “picture bride” to marry my father; she was 18 years old.  By 1942 they had 3 boys during which time my parents were leasing a farm growing flowers in the San Fernando Valley near the corner of Laurel Canyon Blvd. and Montague Street in an area called Pacoima."
