          "type": "sidebar",
          "title": "Archival Note",
          "html": "<p><em><strong>SIDEBAR</strong></em><em>:   Tule Lake concentration camp was labeled as a “segregation center” where the government segregated all those who “failed” the Loyalty Questionnaire, those whom the government considered to be disloyal or trouble-makers.  I question the wisdom of concentrating 15,000 people who were considered to be disloyal or trouble-makers and putting them all into one camp – it should have been expected such a grouping would ultimately foment unrest and make trouble.  Tule Lake is the only center to have a stockade, a prison within the </em><em>prison, to house the so-called trouble-makers and remained throughout the war under strict military security.</em></p>",
          "text": "SIDEBAR:   Tule Lake concentration camp was labeled as a “segregation center” where the government segregated all those who “failed” the Loyalty Questionnaire, those whom the government considered to be disloyal or trouble-makers.  I question the wisdom of concentrating 15,000 people who were considered to be disloyal or trouble-makers and putting them all into one camp – it should have been expected such a grouping would ultimately foment unrest and make trouble.  Tule Lake is the only center to have a stockade, a prison within the prison, to house the so-called trouble-makers and remained throughout the war under strict military security."
