          "text": "After becoming the Executive Director at LTSC in 1980, I had heard from various sources that it was Mayor Tom Bradley who had first expressed the vision to renovate the Old Union Church for the East West Players (EWP) theater.  At that time, EWP was operating a small 99-seat black-box theater in the Silver Lake/Echo Park neighborhood.  To spur the proposed project forward, Mayor Bradley ear-marked $500K for the renovation work – and challenged the EWP to raise the balance (approximately another $500K at the time) for the necessary upgrades and seismic work to convert the church into a theater space."
