          "text": "EWP is considered the “nation’s premiere Asian American live-theater organization” and was deserving of a larger venue that could attract bigger audiences and provide a larger stage for their productions.  I had seen several of their shows at the small theater (including a wonderful production of Stephen Sondheim’s musical play “Pacific Overtures”) and their use of stage production at such a small facility was absolutely amazing.  I whole-heartedly supported the idea of having EWP move into the old Union Church building and becoming a part of Little Tokyo."
