          "text": "EWP, after years of trying to fundraise for the renovation, decided their future lay in finding a theater site in Hollywood rather than in Little Tokyo.  This made some sense since Hollywood is a mecca for drama and acting groups to settle in.  They also felt Little Tokyo was too “Japanese-oriented” while EWP was an Asian American program, so they gave up the idea of moving into the old church.  When I found out EWP was planning to give up on the church site, I asked EWP if LTSC could take over the project, and use the ear-marked funds from Mayor Bradley; they wished us good luck and left the project in our hands.  Even though LTSC had successfully finished the affordable housing project at the Firm Building, nevertheless a theater renovation project was a much different animal than housing."
