          "text": "During the heydays of Little Tokyo (the period between 1910 – 1940), the community became the largest Japanese American enclave in the country which was now populated by young families – as I had mentioned in the section about building a gym in Little Tokyo.  Little Tokyo went through some difficult times after the WW2 incarceration period when all the folks of Japanese ancestry were removed from Little Tokyo and the area became an African American neighborhood which the newcomers called “Bronzeville” during the war period."
