          "text": "As downtown LA and Little Tokyo became more “hip and popular” there was a growing concern about gentrification and its impact on the small businesses in Little Tokyo.  Will the small businesses, especially the legacy businesses that have been in operation by family ownership for generations, be pushed out due to rapidly increased rents?  What could be done to combat the strong economic forces behind gentrification?"
