          "text": "At this same time, a Metro subway connector was slated to open a train station in Little Tokyo in 2023 and this would exacerbate the gentrification forces at work.  It was feared that property values will inevitably rise as well as commercial rents for the small business operators.  Could this spell the doom for the future of Little Tokyo as a “real” cultural and ethnic neighborhood composed of businesses, residents, churches and nonprofits?  We did not want phony building façades like something from Disney World’s EPCOT center.   The Ties That Bind conference that brought out hundreds of JA’s in 1998 to discuss the future of Little Tokyo challenged us to find ways as a community to help support and promote the cultural small businesses and programs that makes Little Tokyo what it has historically been and needs to be.  What could the community do to offset the impact of gentrification?"
